{"ruling":{"ruling":"PARTIAL_REFUND","amount_sgd":9.8,"driver_compensation_sgd":null,"referrals":[],"confidence":0.95,"explanation":"To the rider: your route-deviation claim succeeds in part. The governing measurement is the GPS trace, EV-GPS-00507 (weight 1.0), which records 11.36 km between the recorded pickup at Changi Airport T3 and the dropoff on Nicoll Drive, against the booked optimal route of 3.6 km on the trip record, EV-TRIP-00507 (weight 1.0). The excess is 7.76 km, or 215.6% of optimal: both POL-RD-01 tests pass (greater than 0.8 km and greater than 20%), so the deviation is ESTABLISHED, and it is additionally MATERIAL on the percentage limb. Nothing on the record excuses it. The chat log, EV-CHAT-00507, holds zero messages (trip record chat_message_count 0), so no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 can be run; the trip record shows pickup_amended_at, dropoff_amended_at and amended_optimal_distance_km all null, so POL-RD-05 gives nothing; the vehicle is RYDE_TAXI, so POL-RD-12 does not re-base the threshold; and the fare is METERED with no quoted fare, so POL-RD-11 does not apply. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00507-01 is MISSING, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, and no advisory covers this window, so POL-RD-03 cannot be satisfied and, under POL-RD-13, the driver's account of an external cause carries no weight; because no party cites a traffic cause, the gap is a bundle gap and not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation. The driver's statement that he 'chose a quiet spot' is an account with no artifact behind it and is discarded under POL-RD-08.

To the driver: the finding rests on this trip's own trace, not on your record. The POL-RD-06 profile check comes back clean - deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 250, a ratio of 0.00 - so no repeat pattern is established, no FULL_REFUND uplift is licensed and no driver-conduct referral arises. The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not the field POL-RD-06 names and was not used.

The money under POL-RD-02 (metered fare): charged_total 25.03; recomputed_fare 15.26 = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 3.6 km + 0.28 x 7.0 min) x the surge multiplier of 1.0 read from the fare breakdown EV-FARE-00507 + 0.80 platform fee + 6.00 airport surcharge + 0.00 ERP/tolls, with no waiting fee or promo. The 6.00 surcharge is properly chargeable because the trip ORIGINATED at Changi T3 and ran off-peak (Wednesday), so it is not a billing-integrity defect. Refund = 25.03 - 15.26 = 9.77 before rounding, rounded UP to 9.80. That is 39.0% of the charge, above the 0.50 de minimis and below the 90% full-refund share, so the outcome is a partial refund. No pass-through correction is added: erp_gantries is empty and tolls_erp is 0.00, and POL-RD-09(1) forbids topping up the POL-RD-02 figure. No driver compensation: the distance billed (11.4 km) exceeds the trace (11.36 km), so there are no unbilled kilometres. No escalation trigger fires - identifiers match, the trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) (127 fixes at a 10 s interval, no gaps, max gap 0.0 s), timestamps agree, the refund is far below SGD 150.00, and every charge line has a counterpart. Confidence 0.95, within the cap of 1.0 set by the deciding artifacts, all at weight 1.0."},"discarded_claims":[]}

